    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d583">

                <pb facs="0635" n="585" xml:id="pg585"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-28"><hi rendition="#italic">December 28,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 75.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with Department’s instruction
                    No. 65, of the 9th instant, I herewith transmit for your information a copy of a
                    letter of December 21 last, from Mr. S. C. Neale, covering a decision of the
                    committee of arbitration in the matter of the fine of $2,400 imposed on the
                    American steamer <hi rendition="#italic">City of Washington</hi> at Havana for
                    mere clerical error in the vessel’s manifest.</p>
                <p>You will accordingly bring this decision to the attention of the minister for
                    foreign affairs, to the end that his Government may see the unwarranted action
                    on the part of the officials at Havana in imposing fines for errors so simple
                    and so evidently unintentional.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d583-a1.xml" xpointer="d583-a1"/>
